T042: all registered demos on a fresh demo stack
------------------------------------------------

Which demos run

Only demos 2 (component-overrides) and 3 (backup-restore) are registered in backend/tests/e2e/demos/catalog.py, so 'uv run invoke record' runs those two. Two demos are not registered yet:

- Demo 1 (deploy-upgrade) waits for issue #372 (see spike-notes.md).
- Demo 4 (clone) waits for issue #530, the product fix decided in T008 (see e2e-evidence.md).

The expected result is therefore two 'recorded' lines and two videos, not four. The plain command was used instead of '--demo' runs one after the other, because it runs every registered demo.

Fresh demo stack

Three attempts at 'uv run invoke reset' were needed. The first two failed for host reasons outside the demo code:

- 2026-10-18T22:24:18Z, exit code 1: Traefik never became ready. Flannel inside the vCluster crashed with 'Failed to check br_netfilter: stat /proc/sys/net/bridge/bridge-nf-call-iptables: no such file or directory', because the host kernel had not loaded the br_netfilter module. Fixed on the host with 'sudo modprobe br_netfilter'.
- 2026-10-18T22:30:13Z, exit code 1: 'helm upgrade --install styrmin helm/styrmin' failed with 'found in Chart.yaml, but missing in charts/ directory: postgresql, prefect-server, styrmin-agent, velero'. The Styrmin image already existed, so 'uv run invoke start' skipped 'uv run invoke build', which is the task that runs 'helm dependency update'. Fixed by running 'uv run invoke build' (exit code 0).
- 2026-10-18T22:31:56Z, exit code 0, ended 2026-10-18T22:34:48Z: the stack started and printed 'Styrmin demo is ready'.

First recording attempt

Started 2026-10-18T22:34:56Z. Command: uv run invoke record. Exit code: 1.
